  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Initiative &#xE0; accro&#xEE;tre la transparence dans le march&#xE9; africain (AFMI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AFMI&#x2019;s objective is to contribute to the development and deepening of domestic financial markets in Africa.  It has two components: African Financial Markets Data Base and African Development Bond Fund. The grant was approved to support the first component whose expected impact is an improved, available and transparent African fixed income markets data base; harmonization of data from several institutions and quality of financial statistics in Africa. The User Department indicates that slow start up was as a result of technical issues relating to the software. An action plan is in place and the Bank is working on the content with a target to launch the first phase at the Annual Meetings in June 2011. It is expected that the funds from CIDA will be fully disbursed by the second half of 2011 based on an Action Plan that has been developed.
Approved: CAD 121,650 (3.56% disbursed as at December 2010).</narrative>
  </description>
